--
^warning: ignoring
--
TypedDict types are not recognized. TypedDict creates struct-like
types via class syntax or function calls, but our converter treats
them as regular classes without dict semantics. The variable p gets
a class struct type instead of a dict type, so p["x"] fails.
Fix: detect TypedDict in class bases or function calls, create a
dict type with the specified fields, and handle subscript access.
